                  "rrtV2BlockElementsJson": "{\"children\":[[\"paragraph\",{\"numbering\":\"#none\",\"indent-level\":0,\"children\":[[\"text\",{\"value\":\"CASTLEFORD (26 May) ― From the beginning of the next school term, products from textbook publisher Oxley Ltd. \"}],[\"blank\",{\"number\":0}],[\"text\",{\"value\":\" part of the core curriculum in all new Castleford high schools. Oxley has limitedly provided \"}],[\"blank\",{\"number\":0}],[\"text\",{\"value\":\" materials to Castleford schools so far.\"}]]}],[\"paragraph\",{\"numbering\":\"#none\",\"indent-level\":0}],[\"paragraph\",{\"numbering\":\"#none\",\"indent-level\":0,\"children\":[[\"text\",{\"value\":\"The city council members and Oxley representatives are delighted with their steadily developing \"}],[\"blank\",{\"number\":0}],[\"text\",{\"value\":\". According to David Bellamy, Castleford’s mayor, Oxley’s books provide a high level of content, while also being visually engaging. \"}],[\"blank\",{\"number\":0}],[\"text\",{\"value\":\". \\\"Oxley text\"}],[\"text\",{\"value\":\"books are not only well written and organized, but they also incorporate bright colors and fun activities,\\\" noted Mayor Bellamy. \\\"As such, they are ideal for the curious minds of Castleford students.\\\"\"}]]}]]}"
